.TH DANBY-ARMS 1
.SH NAME
danby-arms \- Richardson arms race
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/arms
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Temple/arms
is an interactive live simulation of Richardson arms race.
It integrates the model continuously and redraws its state as parameters or
initial conditions change.
.SH MODEL
A'=aB-fA+g; B'=bA-fB+g.
.PP
a and b are mutual response, f fatigue, and g grievance. A and B are abstract arsenal levels.
.SH DISPLAY
The main phase portrait plots B horizontally and A vertically.  It combines a
direction field, both nullclines, the historical trajectory, the current state,
and the stable equilibrium when it lies in view.  The lower plot uses the same
generic line geometry to show A(t) and B(t).  The compact stock view retains the
weapon metaphor; each block represents 0.025 arsenal units.
.PP
If f^2>ab the display reports stable equilibrium; otherwise mutual response
produces unstable escalation.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the phase portrait to set A and B through inverse plot scales. Four bottom
tracks set both responses, fatigue, and grievance.
.PP
Space pauses or resumes the simulation.  Period advances one displayed step
while paused.  The
.B r
key restores the default initial state and
.B q
or Escape exits.
.SH INTERPRETATION
The quantities are normalized unless physical units are stated explicitly.
The display is a visualization of a low-dimensional differential-equation
model, not an agent simulation or a prediction of a particular real system.
Parameter changes restart the displayed history so trajectories from different
settings are not joined.
.SH NUMERICS
The state is advanced by the general-purpose
.B Numerics
fourth-order Runge-Kutta solver.  Small negative values caused by numerical
roundoff are clamped for nonnegative population and stock models.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/arms.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR numerics (2)
